---
description: Use when writing or changing component or page CSS, including scoped <style> blocks in a .vue file. Do not use for pure layout/markup changes with no new style declaration, or for UnoCSS utility class selection covered by existing usage.
globs:
  - "app/assets/styles/**/*.css"
  - "app/components/**/*.vue"
  - "app/layouts/**/*.vue"
  - "app/pages/**/*.vue"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Reuse an existing custom property from `app/assets/styles/tokens.css` for a
  colour, spacing, radius, or font value before writing a literal (a raw hex
  code, an arbitrary `px`/`rem` value, or a bespoke font stack).
- If a value genuinely has no matching token, add it to `tokens.css` as a named
  custom property first, then consume it — do not introduce a one-off literal
  in component-scoped CSS that duplicates or drifts from an existing token.
- When implementing a specific Figma frame or component, cite the Figma node
  ID in a CSS comment next to the rule it drove (for example
  `/* Figma 144:1370 */`), so a later reviewer can trace the value back to the
  design source without a Figma MCP round-trip.
- Preserve `prefers-reduced-motion` and existing breakpoint conventions already
  used in `app/pages/index.vue` rather than inventing a new breakpoint value or
  animation approach for a single component.
